# metric-soc2-remediation-status.rq
# Inputs: the SOC2 case-study INSTANCE graph (prov:/skos: vocabulary), same
#         graph metric-soc2-evidenced-controls.rq reads.
# Outputs: single row: ?count = COUNT(DISTINCT management-response /
#          remediation-log deliverable entities generated by the Management
#          Response & Remediation phase (skos:notation "AUDIT-REMEDIATION"),
#          per packs/soc2-audit-pack/ontology.ttl's 10-phase SKOS scheme).
# Meaning: COUNT/ASK-shaped by house convention (this crate's SPARQL engine
#          typed-refuses GROUP_CONCAT/SAMPLE aggregates); a COUNT was chosen
#          over ASK because the query-execution helpers this crate's SPARQL
#          layer already exposes (crates/cng/src/bench/roles.rs::
#          metric_count) are wired for SELECT/COUNT rows, not boolean ASK
#          results — reusing that existing helper rather than adding new ASK
#          plumbing. A nonzero count records that remediation evidence has
#          been recorded for the engagement; it is never a claim that every
#          identified exception WAS remediated (that ratio, if wanted, is
#          DERIVED_ARITHMETIC computed in Rust from two measured counts, per
#          crates/cng/src/bench/report.rs's ModeledLlmComparison/
#          DerivedScaleExtrapolation convention — see
#          crates/cng/src/bench/soc2.rs::Soc2EvidenceMetrics) — and never a
#          compliance verdict. See soc2.rs's module doc for the full
#          COMPLIANCE-OVERCLAIM FENCE.
# Determinism: aggregate over a fixed graph; single row needs no ORDER BY,
# one is present for uniformity.
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
PREFIX prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>

SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?remediationArtifact) AS ?count)
WHERE {
  ?phase a prov:Activity ;
         skos:notation "AUDIT-REMEDIATION" ;
         prov:generated ?remediationArtifact .
  ?remediationArtifact a prov:Entity .
}
ORDER BY ?count
